For the purposes of this Act, there is established a fund to be known as the Maritime and Port Authority of Brunei Darussalam Fund into which

(a) such sums as may be paid to the Authority out of the Consolidated Fund;

(b) such sums as may be raised by the Authority by loan;

(c) all rents and proceeds of sale profits and income and other revenue derived by the Authority directly or indirectly from the property belonging to the Authority;

(d) all such other sums as may be paid to the Authority. Application of Fund

(1) The Fund for any financial year shall be applied in defraying the following charges

(a) the remuneration, fees and allowances of the members of the a

(b) the salaries, fees, remuneration, superannuation allowances and gratuities of the officers, agents, employees, advisers and former employees of the Authority or its predecessors;

(c) working and establishment expenses and expenditure on, or provision for, the maintenance of any of the property of the Authority, and the discharge of the functions of the Authority properly chargeable to the Fund;

(d) interest on any debentures issued and on any loan raised by Authority of Brunei Darussalanz CAP. 222 27

